  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "What pipelock checks",
      "items": [
        "Destination of every proxied request: paste and file-drop blocklist, private and cloud-metadata addresses, data hidden in host names, 1200 requests per minute per site",
        "letta-code's own calls too: a model server on a private address is refused unless it is in PIPELOCK_DIRECT or is host.docker.internal",
        "Page text and full URL only for pages read through /fetch (the fetching-web-pages skill); a page with prompt injection is blocked with a 403",
        "Every allow and block is a hash-chained receipt signed with the stack's own Ed25519 key"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "What it does not do",
      "items": [
        "Advisory, not a boundary: the stack network still reaches the internet, and any agent can unset HTTPS_PROXY",
        "No TLS interception: for HTTPS it sees the host name, not paths, bodies or responses",
        "The BFF (its Remote Pi SSH runs included), garden-vault, google-mcp, garden-gmail-triggers, garden-watchlist and the Telegram gateway connect directly; NO_PROXY also keeps searxng, ddg-mcp, gotenberg, host.docker.internal and the hosts in PIPELOCK_DIRECT direct"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Guarded by lettucectl check",
      "items": [
        "garden-pipelock hardened: read-only, no capabilities, no host mounts",
        "Only garden-pipelock mounts pipelock-data, whatever the profiles",
        "The app-server's proxy variables point at garden-pipelock, and its NO_PROXY lists garden-vault, garden-gmail-triggers, garden-watchlist and garden, so pipelock never sees the vault's values or the executor's token"
      ]
    }
  ]
